\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The Spatial Election Explorer (SEE) synthetic data interface. Voters (blue) and candidates (orange) are embedded in a 2D issue space (left); the interface lets the user place points manually, sample from synthetic distributions, load survey-grounded data, manage stacked data layers, and run an election under a chosen voting rule. \textbf  {(A)} Abstract 2D election space; (unitless, $[0,1]$). \textbf  {(B)} Voter (blue dot). \textbf  {(C)} Candidate (orange star). Winners are rendered at full opacity; eliminated candidates are dimmed in place. \textbf  {(D)} Gaussian sampling distribution, drawn as concentric $1\sigma $/$2\sigma $/$3\sigma $ contours. \textbf  {(E)} Top bar: add voters or candidates by hand, launch the tutorial, import or export the current configuration. \textbf  {(F)} Tabs switch between synthetic (\S  \ref {sub:Input}) and survey data exploration (\S  \ref {sub:Survey Data}). \textbf  {(G)} Synthetic distribution configuration, and click ``add data'' to drop the sampled points onto the plot (\S  \ref {sub:Input}). \textbf  {(H)} Each manual point or sampled distribution is a stackable, editable layer (\S  \ref {sub:Plot Management}). \textbf  {(I)} Choose voting rule (Plurality, Borda, IRV, Bloc Plurality, STV, SNTV) and number of winners, then run the election.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{The Spatial Election Explorer (SEE) synthetic data interface. Voters (blue) and candidates (orange) are embedded in a 2D issue space (left); the interface lets the user place points manually, sample from synthetic distributions, load survey-grounded data, manage stacked data layers, and run an election under a chosen voting rule. \textbf {(A)} Abstract 2D election space; (unitless, $[0,1]$). \textbf {(B)} Voter (blue dot). \textbf {(C)} Candidate (orange star). Winners are rendered at full opacity; eliminated candidates are dimmed in place. \textbf {(D)} Gaussian sampling distribution, drawn as concentric $1\sigma $/$2\sigma $/$3\sigma $ contours. \textbf {(E)} Top bar: add voters or candidates by hand, launch the tutorial, import or export the current configuration. \textbf {(F)} Tabs switch between synthetic (\S \ref {sub:Input}) and survey data exploration (\S \ref {sub:Survey Data}). \textbf {(G)} Synthetic distribution configuration, and click ``add data'' to drop the sampled points onto the plot (\S \ref {sub:Input}). \textbf {(H)} Each manual point or sampled distribution is a stackable, editable layer (\S \ref {sub:Plot Management}). \textbf {(I)} Choose voting rule (Plurality, Borda, IRV, Bloc Plurality, STV, SNTV) and number of winners, then run the election}{figure.1}{}}
